---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_URL, MINIMUM_AGE, TERMS_EFFECTIVE, TERMS_VERSION } from '../lib/legal';
---

<Base title="Terms of Use">
  <div class="legal">
    <header class="hero">
      <h1 class="page-title">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="version">Version {TERMS_VERSION}, effective {TERMS_EFFECTIVE}</p>
      <p class="lede">
        ResearchScout is a personal, non-commercial research radar run by one person. These
        terms were written from what the software actually does. They are not legal advice, and
        they are deliberately short.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>1. Accepting these terms</h2>
      <p>
        Using the site means accepting these terms. Creating an account means accepting them
        explicitly, which the site asks you to do once, and again if they change in a way that
        needs a new version.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>2. Who may use it</h2>
      <p>
        You must be at least {MINIMUM_AGE} years old. One account per person. Keep your login
        credentials to yourself; anything done through your account is treated as done by you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>3. What you may and may not do</h2>
      <p>
        Read, search, save papers, and ask questions. That is what it is for. Please do not:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          extract the catalogue in bulk, or use automated tools to page through it beyond
          ordinary reading;
        </li>
        <li>
          work around rate limits, access controls, or the sign-in requirement on any feature;
        </li>
        <li>
          resell, redistribute or republish the data this site collects from its sources, which
          the sources' own licenses do not permit;
        </li>
        <li>use the site to break the law, or to attack, overload or probe the systems behind it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The upstream data is available directly from arXiv, Semantic Scholar and the other
        sources listed on the <a href="/about">about page</a>, under their own terms. Go to them
        rather than scraping this site.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>4. The papers are not ours</h2>
      <p>
        Paper metadata comes from arXiv under a CC0 public domain dedication. The papers
        themselves stay under their authors' copyright and whichever license each author chose.
        This site links to originals, quotes at most a few hundred characters with attribution,
        and never redistributes PDFs or source files. Citation data comes from Semantic Scholar
        and is used non-commercially with attribution, as its license requires.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are an author or rights holder and something here is wrong or should not be here,{' '}
        <a href={CONTACT_URL} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">open an issue</a> and it
        will be corrected or removed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>5. Machine-generated text</h2>
      <p>
        Summaries, topic labels, digests and Scout's answers are produced by a language model
        from stored abstracts and short excerpts. They can be wrong, incomplete or misleading,
        and a momentum score measures attention rather than quality. Nothing here is research,
        medical, legal or financial advice. Read the paper before relying on anything.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>6. Availability</h2>
      <p>
        The backend runs on one machine in the operator's home. The site will be unavailable at
        times - a reboot, an update, a power cut - sometimes without warning, and it may be
        discontinued. There is no service level, no support commitment, and no guarantee that
        data you store here will survive. Export anything you care about.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>7. Your account and your data</h2>
      <p>
        You keep your own interests, saved lists and reading history; the site uses them only to
        run the service and personalize what it shows you, as described in the{' '}
        <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>. You can export or delete everything from your
        profile at any time. Deleting your account removes your login and every row tied to it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>8. Ending it</h2>
      <p>
        You may delete your account whenever you like. Accounts that abuse the site, break these
        terms, or endanger the systems behind it may be suspended or removed without notice.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>9. No warranty, and limits on liability</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided as is, without warranties of any kind, to the fullest extent the
        law allows. The operator is not liable for any indirect, incidental or consequential
        loss arising from using it, or from relying on anything it says. Nothing here limits
        liability that cannot lawfully be limited.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>10. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        These terms carry a version. Substantive changes get a new version and the site asks
        you to accept it on your next visit; the current one is shown at the top of this page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>11. Law and contact</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the law of the United States and of the state where the
        operator resides, without regard to conflict-of-law rules. Questions, corrections and
        complaints go to{' '}
        <a href={CONTACT_URL} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">the project's issue
        tracker</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 58rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .hero {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .hero .page-title {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }
  .version {
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  .lede {
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .block {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    padding-top: var(--space-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .block h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .block p,
  .block ul {
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin: 0 auto 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .block ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }
  .block li {
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
  }
  .block p:last-child,
  .block ul:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
